                        "unit": "ml",
                        "optional": 0
                    }
                ],
                "steps": [
                    {
                        "step": "Dissolve ingredients except sulfur, yeast extract, vitamins and sulfide, then adjust the pH to 3.5 with 4 N H2SO4. Sparge medium with 100% N2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic, then dispense under same gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials which contain already the appropriate amount of sulfur, only to 30% of their volume to allow for a large headspace. Autoclave at <b>105\u00b0C</b> for 20 min. Prior to inoculation add yeast extract, vitamins (sterilized by filtration) and sulfide from anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas atmosphere. The final pH of the complete medium should be around 4.0."
                    },
                    {
                        "step": "After inoculation, pressurize the cultivation vessels to 1 bar overpressure with sterile 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture."
                    }
                ],
                "equipment": {
                    "1051": "Filter",
                    "3055": "Autoclave",
                    "3859": "Hungate tubes",
                    "4463": "Gassing station"
                }
